\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Gate operating characteristic: committed-rate difference minimax $-$ uniform vs.\ $\tau $ ($G{=}4$, $R{=}1200$, $20$ seeds, same paired-MPB certificate). The driver is the \emph  {deployed set}: non-spanning $W'$ gives minimax a strict committed-rate advantage at both variance levels; spanning $W$ makes them equal at low $\mathrm  {CV}$ and \emph  {reverses} the order at high $\tau $ (minimax starves low-variance vertices). Evidence: \texttt  {results/SUBGMIX\_GATE\_OC\_R1899.json}.}}{12}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:gateoc}{{8}{12}{Gate operating characteristic: committed-rate difference minimax $-$ uniform vs.\^^M$\tau $ ($G{=}4$, $R{=}1200$, $20$ seeds, same paired-MPB certificate). The driver is the \emph {deployed set}: non-spanning $W'$ gives minimax a strict committed-rate advantage at both variance levels; spanning $W$ makes them equal at low $\mathrm {CV}$ and \emph {reverses} the order at high $\tau $ (minimax starves low-variance vertices). Evidence: \texttt {results/SUBGMIX\_GATE\_OC\_R1899.json}}{table.8}{}}
