\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Certificate-time emptiness is a provable function of the label budget.} (a) The $125$ real-switch rows ($i^\star \!\ne  \!F_0$) at the full split across the fresh seeds $\{10,\dots  ,14\}$, in the \emph  {selector-margin $\Delta (w)$ vs.\ required bandwidth-mass $B{=}\Delta \sqrt  {b^\star (w)}$} quadrant (log-log; marker keyed by carrier). Admission under any strictly finite-sample band forces $\Delta (w)\ge B$ (the feasible half-plane below the dashed $\Delta {=}B$ line); every realized row lies strictly above it, i.e.\ its certified emptiness $b^\star (w)\!>\!1$ is \emph  {provable} over the whole feasible axis, not merely observed. (b) The deployable \emph  {absolute} exact gate (M2.5) instead retains content monotonically in the label budget $b$: committed rate grows with $b$ on fashion/digits while mnist commits at every budget, all with unit no-worse-than-$F_0$ coverage (Sec.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:tau}). The relative gate (M6) is an asymptotic/descriptive diagnostic only.}}{14}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:m10frontier}{{1}{14}{\textbf {Certificate-time emptiness is a provable function of the label budget.} (a) The $125$ real-switch rows ($i^\star \!\ne \!F_0$) at the full split across the fresh seeds $\{10,\dots ,14\}$, in the \emph {selector-margin $\Delta (w)$ vs.\ required bandwidth-mass $B{=}\Delta \sqrt {b^\star (w)}$} quadrant (log-log; marker keyed by carrier). Admission under any strictly finite-sample band forces $\Delta (w)\ge B$ (the feasible half-plane below the dashed $\Delta {=}B$ line); every realized row lies strictly above it, i.e.\ its certified emptiness $b^\star (w)\!>\!1$ is \emph {provable} over the whole feasible axis, not merely observed. (b) The deployable \emph {absolute} exact gate (M2.5) instead retains content monotonically in the label budget $b$: committed rate grows with $b$ on fashion/digits while mnist commits at every budget, all with unit no-worse-than-$F_0$ coverage (Sec.~\ref {app:tau}). The relative gate (M6) is an asymptotic/descriptive diagnostic only}{figure.1}{}}
